Question #9:

In this challenge, you used rank() to determine standing and order() to determine display order.

Could you have used order() alone to solve the entire problem (both awarding ranks AND reordering the table)? 

  No, I could not have used order() alone to solve the entire problem because it cannot properly award ranks to the employees.
  

Explain what order() is missing that rank() provides, using your own words rather than repeating the definitions

  The order() function only finds the row spots needed to line the table up from top to bottom, which forces one person to be placed ahead of another even if they sold the exact same amount. It is missing the ability to compare the actual sales numbers to see how well everyone did against each other, which rank() provides by giving a fair placement score and properly showing when two people are tied for the same spot.



